						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, April 12, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">FORGET the Old World!! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Empire of Eternity is currently recruiting new members who are interested in raiding/grouping in PoPower, Luclin, LDoN hard setting and GoDiscord. Must be level 62+, working on or have Emp SSRA/VThal key, a computer that doesn't lag out when raiding, a good attitude and a stable personal life. You must download and use Teamspeak during raids. (We don't like typing) A headset with microphone attached is preferred. We are number 9 on your right, click to enter our website and PST to any member in-game to inquire about joining the Empire!
							<br><BR>
							 - jenbobo<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=513">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Saturday, April 10, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">199 Black Reavers in CoM </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Last night Sacred Honor took a trek to CoM.  Only reason for going was to finish Stogard's Shaman Epic.  I have finally found the trick to getting those Jade Reavers out of the Black Reavers!  Don't go with any intention of getting one, go for a different item!<BR><BR>Anyway, Rak was sitting up in the room off the lift.  Somehow, while scouting, we ended up with 3 reavers at once.  Being only eight of us, it was a hard pull and on that final reaver came the one after another spawn...  2 more guildies showed up midway through the count for the Rak kill and helped dispense with these beasts.<BR><BR>When all was said and done, 199 reavers dead, 16 Jade Reavers dropped, 4 deaths in the group were incurred and Stoggie finished his epic!<BR><BR>Sun Clan move over, we took our record back!  hehehehe  *teases*
							<br><BR>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=512">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Tuesday, April 06, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Chaotic Killers Recruiting </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Clan of Chaotic Killers is now Recruiting! We are a 55+ guild that's seeking adventurers of all classes presently.  More information can be found at ChaoticKillers.com
							<br><BR>
							 - Kilila<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=511">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Sunday, April 04, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">LOG IN SERVER RESCUE! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							I took this from the EQLIVE.COM tech portion of the Forums...<BR><BR>This is what worked for me, on right now.<BR>{copy and pasted from eqlive boards}<BR><BR>OK here comes the RESCUE.<BR><BR>I logged in but has to do like this.<BR><BR>1 RUN EQ patcher.<BR><BR>2. Stay at the patcher screen and OPEN the EQHOST.TXT with text editor.<BR><BR>3. chaged text inside EQHOST.TXT like this:<BR><BR>{Registration Servers]<BR>{<BR>"eqlogin1.989studios.com:5999"<BR>}<BR>[Login Servers]<BR>{<BR>"eqlogin3.989studios.com:15900"<BR>"eqlogin3.989studios.com:15901"<BR>"eqlogin3.989studios.com:15902"<BR>"eqlogin3.989studios.com:15903"<BR>}<BR><BR>4. NOW save the file. THEN hit PLAY. Enjoy . I am in already : )))) 
							<br><BR>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=510">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=510">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><BR><img src=images/redline.gif height=2 width="100%"><BR><BR></TD></TR>
					

						<TR><TD><p class="pTitle">Sistinas recruiting </p></TD></TR>
							<TR><TD><p class=pText>
							Do you have what it takes to be a part of Sistinas?  Here is a list of requirements<BR><BR>Cleric          lvl 40+   High Need  (15 hours a week minimum play time)<BR><BR>Wizard        lvl 45+   High Need  (15 hours a week minimum play time)<BR><BR>Enchanter    lvl 45+   Med Need  (15 hours a week minimum play time)<BR><BR>Warrior       lvl 50+   Low Need  (20 hours a week minimum play time)<BR><BR>Paladin        lvl 45+   High Need  (15 hours a week minimum play time)<BR><BR>Beast           lvl 50+   Low Need  (20 hours a week minimum play time)<BR><BR>Mage          lvl 40+    High Need  (15 hours a week minimum play time)<BR><BR>SK             lvl 50+    High Need  (15 hours a week minimum play time)<BR><BR>Druid          lvl 50+   Low Need  (20 hours a week minimum play time)<BR><BR>Necro         lvl 40+   High Need  (15 hours a week minimum play time)<BR><BR>If interested put in an application some exceptions may be made based on the amount of play time a person has to play their character. All classes must make 1 raid a week either on friday/saturday/ or sunday afternoon/night.<BR><BR>You must also be willing to help out guild members, stick with 1 guild we dont want guild hoppers, and enjoy playing with others that love the game. Sistinas is a family we stick together through good and bad if you meet these requirements welcome to the Sistinas family =P<BR><BR>Exarch Yates Arcaneforce<BR><BR>65th lvl cleric (162AA)<BR><BR>Guild Leader<BR><BR>Any questions e-mail me at Yates@sistinas.Eliteguilds.com<BR>
							 <BR><BR>- sistinas<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=509">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, April 02, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Join the Knights of Nobility! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							 Knights of Nobility Accepting New Members<BR><BR>As the winds of chaos died, only a few remained to stand strong against the darkness. They were deemed the Knights of Nobility by Mithaniel Marr himself.<BR><BR>Knights of Nobility seeks to shed light upon the inhabitants of Norrath and its heavens by banding together to facilitate hunting parties, protect each other from evil forces, and share our wealth of knowledge with each other.<BR><BR>If you are seeking a guild that is more interested in adventuring and exploring than being "uber", that doesn't require you to play a certain number of hours a week, likes to do a bit of roleplaying (nothing too strict), and that brings together like-minded players that enjoy all facets of the game (not just leveling), then we may be the guild for you!<BR><BR>Check out our website by clicking on the "Guilds" link on the left and make yourself known to us in our message forum!<BR><BR>Honor virutus preamium!<BR>Honor is the reward of virtue!
							<br><BR>
							 - Tuwini<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=508">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Wednesday, March 31, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Another 10th Ring War </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hi all.  I'd just like to announce I will be forming a raid party to attempt my 10th ring quest.  I plan to have most groups set by 3PM Est or Noon Pst.  Loot will be rolled on by lvl 55+ players, class rolls only.<BR><BR>I am running this raid by myself so any support is more than welcome.  Please make plans to come or at least tell a friend.  Hope to see you there!<BR><BR>Earman Wax  65 Paladin
							<br><BR>
							 - Earman<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=507">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, March 29, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">What's that FUNK? </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							You've seen us around...you've noticed the name...you've thought to yourself "Self, could I be funky too"?  Well we've got good news! <BR><BR>House of Funk is looking for 60+ individuals who want to get down with NToV and Sleepers Tomb.  Speak to us in game or come visit us at www.hofguild.org! <BR><BR>Muse Gilae Sul'delDraug<BR>The Funk Phenomenon 
							<br><BR>
							 - Gilae<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=506">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, March 26, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Join Knights of Nobility! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Knights of Nobility Accepting New Members<BR><BR>As the winds of chaos died, only a few remained to stand strong against the darkness. They were deemed the Knights of Nobility by Mithaniel Marr himself.<BR><BR>Knights of Nobility seeks to shed light upon the inhabitants of Norrath and its heavens by banding together to facilitate hunting parties, protect each other from evil forces, and share our wealth of knowledge with each other.<BR><BR>If you are seeking a guild that is more interested in adventuring and exploring than being "uber", that doesn't require you to play a certain number of hours a week, likes to do a bit of roleplaying (nothing too strict), and that brings together like-minded players that enjoy all facets of the game (not just leveling), then we may be the guild for you!<BR><BR>Check out our website by clicking on the "Guilds" link on the left and make yourself known to us in our message forum!<BR><BR>Honor virutus preamium!<BR>Honor is the reward of virtue!<BR><BR>Sincerely,<BR>Tuwini Tooteeny<BR>Grand Duchess<BR>Knights of Nobility 
							<br><BR>
							 - Tuwini<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=503">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><BR><img src=images/redline.gif height=2 width="100%"><BR><BR></TD></TR>
					

						<TR><TD><p class="pTitle">New Black Reaver Record </p></TD></TR>
							<TR><TD><p class=pText>
							<font face="Comic Sans MS" size="2">A few weeks ago Sun Clan of Warriors took a little journey to City of Mist.  They went to say Hi to a few Black Reavers and entice them into giving up a few Jade Reavers.<BR>From the desk of Nyfeara:<BR>The last guy was #196, 12 jade reavers dropped.<BR><BR>Sacred Honor's record BROKE!  I told Ny at one point, "Ok you guys can stop now, you broke Our record!"<BR><BR>We had a GM spawn in TD to fix a bug for us and I let her know that YES! There is a new Black Reaver Record!</font><BR><BR><font face="Comic Sans MS" size="4">CONGRATS to my Friends over at SUN CLAN for the NEW SERVER RECORD!</font>
							 <BR><BR>- Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=502">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp; <a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=502">[View Comments]</a>

					<BR><BR></TD></TR>

